# Help topic "What is running, and why it is busy": paragraph 3.
settings-help-topics-activity-p3 = All the parts of a program are added together, so Firefox is one bubble however many tabs it has. Two quiet gray bubbles hold the rest: Trindle desktop, which is everything Trindle runs to be the desktop, and Linux and other programs. Trindle's apps, such as Settings and Apps, count as programs, not as the desktop.

# Help topic "What is running, and why it is busy": paragraph 4.
settings-help-topics-activity-p4 = Down the side, four rings show the memory, the processor, the disk and the swap file; on a computer with no swap file the last one shows the processor's temperature instead. In the memory ring, Trindle's own share is in the highlight color, and your programs and Linux are in blue.

# Help topic "What is running, and why it is busy": step 2 of the numbered steps at block 5.
settings-help-topics-activity-step5-2 = Press the stop button on the card. It fills with the highlight color and shows a tick.

